--- MESSAGE ---
A rule's pattern and action are functions, and Java's Consumer leaves the definition

Rule and RuleType declare `pattern (Knowledge -> Unit)` and `action (RhsContext -> Unit)`, both arguments
draco.rete's own wrap types, and a pattern is applied, `pattern(knowledge)`. Java's Consumer was in the
definition because Evrete is Java and its `execute` refuses a Scala function value; a lambda literal
converts there, as the generated action already relied on, so the Scala target writes `execute
(action(_))` at that one call and names the interface nowhere else. Twenty rule projections lose the
import; twenty call sites apply instead of accept.

